      "title": "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Circle"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1c305ec8-1ab4-5367-bead-5280fcb57508",
      ":question/problem": "![](/tmp/course-academy-g2-readonly-tly0pcma/17592186166865/caller-easy/generated/50c228992ce25be351b7233d.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "69dd3f5f-49a1-591a-ae98-0d64ab2a6640",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "7433bef1-c84d-5596-bf4a-affb9dec4181",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{x}{y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "afe4e3e3-5d13-59fa-ab53-8a28c2d0efe1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{2x}{y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "8dd45d19-3fec-5727-b15c-0d417fe486be",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{y}{x}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "49588500-6c1f-5ac2-83eb-af2ad00edf95",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{x}{2y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "0bf9e76a-ce74-5dcb-b313-556fe3d93f0e",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{x}{y}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "7433bef1-c84d-5596-bf4a-affb9dec4181"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since our circle is centered at the origin and has a radius of $5,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={5}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(25) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
